  "id": "Compound::DB00549 - Gene::1558",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Zafirlukast and Cyp2c8 through multiple interconnected pathways. Zafirlukast, a leukotriene receptor antagonist, is involved in the metabolic pathway of diclofenac, which is processed by Cyp2c8. This indicates that Zafirlukast may influence the activity of Cyp2c8 through its role in the metabolic processes of diclofenac. Additionally, Zafirlukast is included in the category of organonitrogen heterocyclic compounds and is associated with anti-asthmatic agents, which may contribute to its interaction with Cyp2c8. The evidence also highlights that Zafirlukast can cause allergic granulomatous angiitis, which is linked to Montelukast, further suggesting a possible mechanism by which Zafirlukast interacts with Cyp2c8. The integration of these pathways suggests that Zafirlukast may modulate Cyp2c8 activity through metabolic and pharmacological mechanisms, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
